From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:48:33 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: translate the P1 interface strings at the ribbon, menu, dialog and backstage helpers

Routes the interface text that Phase 1 translates through i18n::t() at the display sites, with no
change to any label, id or command: the ribbon tab row and the helpers big(), small(), tip() and
menu_item(); the command palette labels; the dialog title, the OK/Cancel buttons, dialog field
labels and the About blurb; the Backstage helpers (side-menu entries, page heading, heading, dim,
arrow_link, the search hint, tiles, square buttons, place rows, tasks), the Appearance dropdown and
the former rebrand("...") sites, which now go through t() (it rebrands too). With English selected,
or without catalogs, every string is what it was. Strings that do not reach these helpers stay
English until a later phase wraps them; the catalog can already hold any string that does.
